DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eetthheerr__ggeenn__aaddddrr() function generates an arbitrary MAC address for use
     by an ethernet interface that does not have an assigned address.

     By default, eetthheerr__ggeenn__aaddddrr attempts to generate a stable MAC address us‐
     ing the hostid of the jail that the _i_f_p is being added to.  During early
     boot, the hostid may not be set on machines that haven't yet populated
     _/_e_t_c_/_h_o_s_t_i_d, or on machines that do not use loader(8).

     eetthheerr__ggeenn__aaddddrr can fail to derive a MAC address due to memory allocation
     failure, or because the hostid has not been populated.  In these cases, a
     locally-administered unicast MAC address will be randomly generated and
     returned via the _h_w_a_d_d_r parameter.

     If eetthheerr__ggeenn__aaddddrr succeeds, then it will return a MAC address in the
     FreeBSD Foundation OUI, “58:9c:fc”, via the _h_w_a_d_d_r parameter.

